    {
      "id": "section:6/block:18/seg:0",
      "source": "Since Linux 5.0, all three are unified — `synchronize_rcu()` waits for all three simultaneously.",
      "source_hash": 3794191100604332796,
      "context_hash": 12897208714631304721,
      "translation": "Linux 5.0부터 세 가지가 모두 통합되었으며, `synchronize_rcu()`는 세 가지 모두를 동시에 기다립니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Linux": "Linux"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863623Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "SRCU: sleepable RCU",
      "source_hash": 17877356675090966814,
      "context_hash": 10062209406755632728,
      "translation": "SRCU: 슬립 가능한 RCU",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU",
        "SRCU": "SRCU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863623Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Standard RCU read-side critical sections cannot sleep.",
      "source_hash": 15997267788092427298,
      "context_hash": 3001042391066604010,
      "translation": "표준 RCU 읽기 측 임계 구역(critical section)에서는 슬립할 수 없습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU",
        "critical sections": "임계 구역"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863623Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "SRCU (Sleepable RCU) lifts this restriction at the cost of higher read-side overhead:",
      "source_hash": 3813169056807273890,
      "context_hash": 17319633458399420760,
      "translation": "SRCU(Sleepable RCU)는 읽기 측 오버헤드가 더 커지는 대신 이 제약을 없앱니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU",
        "SRCU": "SRCU",
        "overhead": "오버헤드"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863624Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:7/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "SRCU is used where readers need to sleep, such as notifier chains, filesystem operations, and BPF program invocation.",
      "source_hash": 2739512069114260275,
      "context_hash": 549541882454757405,
      "translation": "SRCU는 notifier chain, 파일시스템 연산, BPF 프로그램 호출처럼 읽기 측이 슬립해야 하는 곳에서 사용됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "BPF program": "BPF 프로그램",
        "SRCU": "SRCU",
        "notifier": "notifier"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863624Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:8/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "When to use RCU",
      "source_hash": 8787945839810589418,
      "context_hash": 14652070237246406772,
      "translation": "RCU를 사용해야 하는 경우",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863624Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Tree RCU: grace period detection mechanism",
      "source_hash": 16711309803966021831,
      "context_hash": 12989177424980156220,
      "translation": "Tree RCU: grace period 감지 메커니즘",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU",
        "grace period": "grace period"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863624Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "`synchronize_rcu()` on a real system can't simply \"wait for every CPU to context switch\" — it would block the caller indefinitely on a loaded system.",
      "source_hash": 14539117251793473289,
      "context_hash": 11769239300929990757,
      "translation": "실제 시스템에서 `synchronize_rcu()`는 단순히 \"모든 CPU가 컨텍스트 스위치할 때까지 기다릴\" 수 없습니다. 그렇게 하면 부하가 걸린 시스템에서 호출자가 무기한 블록될 것입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPU": "CPU",
        "context switch": "컨텍스트 스위치"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863624Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Tree RCU solves this with an efficient hierarchical algorithm:",
      "source_hash": 12868246446460120745,
      "context_hash": 2734100554623390648,
      "translation": "Tree RCU는 효율적인 계층적 알고리즘으로 이 문제를 해결합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863625Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "Grace period phases",
      "source_hash": 11828208991606006820,
      "context_hash": 3899006338114686932,
      "translation": "Grace period 단계",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "grace period": "grace period"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863625Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "Expedited grace periods",
      "source_hash": 4921798712068211295,
      "context_hash": 8908557106182409002,
      "translation": "Expedited grace period",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "grace periods": "grace period"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863625Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:6/seg:0",
      "source": "`synchronize_rcu_expedited()` forces a fast grace period by sending IPIs to all CPUs to make them immediately report a quiescent state:",
      "source_hash": 7963142971224792126,
      "context_hash": 6710468575318860030,
      "translation": "`synchronize_rcu_expedited()`는 모든 CPU에 IPI를 보내 즉시 quiescent state를 보고하게 함으로써 grace period를 빠르게 끝내도록 강제합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "CPUs": "CPU",
        "grace period": "grace period"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863625Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:8/seg:0",
      "source": "TASKS RCU",
      "source_hash": 12585040834437828156,
      "context_hash": 4220726140031803678,
      "translation": "TASKS RCU",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863625Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:9/block:9/seg:0",
      "source": "For \"tasks\" (non-atomic, can-sleep contexts), Tasks RCU tracks quiescent states differently:",
      "source_hash": 9126369179165884726,
      "context_hash": 17537069225987306273,
      "translation": "\"태스크\"(원자적이지 않고 슬립할 수 있는 컨텍스트)에 대해 Tasks RCU는 quiescent state를 다른 방식으로 추적합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:57.863625Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:10/block:0/seg:0",
